                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Can see my first impressions here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zcjoHITTjgU\n  \n[h1]Summary[/h1] \n  \nRules of Descruction is interesting. As you read all the time I wish there was a option to say \"Good but not yet\". I like where the game is going but its far from it still. \n  \n[h1]Pros[/h1] \n[list]  \n[*]Good graphics so far.\n[*]Good music, when its there.\n [/list] \n \n[h1]Cons[/h1] \n [list]  \n[*]Some crude animations.\n[*]Music just cuts out randomly.\n[*]Some big frame drops in some areas.\n [/list] \n  \n[h1]My Opinion[/h1]  \n[b]It looks good and plays well for an indie game. That being said I don't think its quite ready yet. Some more polish and sure just not yet.[/b]",
